tool.help:
@EARLY_VERSION@ **What it does**
This tool describes each column of your table, as a first step towards mapping it to FAIRe. For each column, it reports what the values look like: numbers and their range, dates and their format, DNA sequences and their length, ENVO-style labels such as *sea water [ENVO:00002149]*, place names, yes/no values, durations and sequence file names. It also says whether the values differ on every row or are the same on every row.
**FAIRe mapper: propose mapping** uses the same profile to match columns to FAIRe terms, so running this tool on its own is a good way to check how your table has been read.
-----
**Output**
The output has one row for each column of your table. Each row starts with a plain summary, followed by the counts, some example values and the individual measures, such as the fraction of values that are numbers or dates.
The tool treats values such as *NA*, *missing* or *not applicable: control sample* as empty.
@HELP_INPUTS@
@HELP_FAIRE_GUIDE@
@HELP_ABOUT@
